<title>SWITZERLAND: World airfreight traffic up 8pct in Mar 97 - ACI.</title>
<headline>World airfreight traffic up 8pct in Mar 97 - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled by 495 airports around the world in March 1997 totalled more than 4.5 million tonnes, up eight percent on the same month the previous year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions in March 1997, with percentage change on March 1996, was as follows</p>
<p>		     March 1997	    Pct change on Mar 96</p>
<p>Africa	     28,586 tonnes	down  5.2 percent</p>
<p>Asia/Pacific  1,065,830 tonnes	up   16.0</p>
<p>Europe	    943,757 tonnes	up    4.2</p>
<p>LatAm/Carib     103,273 tonnes	down  4.0</p>
<p>Middle East     138,439 tonnes	up   12.6</p>
<p>North America 2,266,261 tonnes	up    6.7</p>
<p>Total	   4,546,146 tonnes	up    8.0</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
<p>www.racs.com</p>
</text>
